{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/776036-how-do-you-play-with-total-darkness","id":776036,"title":"How do you play with \"total darkness\"?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-28T08:33:12-08:00","id":776036,"title":"How do you play with \"total darkness\"?","content":"Some powers talk about &quot;total&quot; or &quot;complete&quot; darkness, and in my experience this isn't that common. I've been in a cave when they shut the lights out, that's total darkness. I've lived in both the country and city, total darkness doesn't really exist in either, there is simply too much light pollution even when the lights are turned out. You might not even believe what you can see in the wilderness when the lights are out and there is no artificial lighting.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it is simply because I'm not spending enough time thinking about how a Vampiric lair would have to have its windows covered to protect from sunlight. As a GM it would seem unfair to either players or me with NPCs to restrict these abilities to reflect reality, yet maybe they should be.<br /> <br /> For example<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Strix can take an area of complete darkness and make it<br /> more, deepening it until it is no longer the simple absence of<br /> light but a gateway to wherever the Strix first came from.<br /> Creating the gateway requires a total lack of illumination in an<br /> area of at least a cubic yard (or meter). </div> </div> </div>if there were any illumination anywhere it would be impossible to have an area with a &quot;total lack&quot;, because light bounces around (or works as waves I think, photons and all that). Strix vision is not inhibited (same with khaibit), yada yada.<br /> <br /> <br /> How do you address this in your games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T12:06:00-08:00","id":776123,"title":"","content":"I hadn't even thought of it, but I wouldn't stress it. No artificial lighting? No visible stars? Close enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T12:38:28-08:00","id":776144,"title":"","content":"Yeah, actual total darkness is pretty rare above ground. I'd say there are two ways to handle this. Either do as dxanders suggests and treat &quot;no illumination&quot; as actually meaning &quot;no <i>direct</i> illumination (natural or artificial)&quot;, or you could assume that the power is meant to require some setup to use. Either seems perfectly reasonable to me.<br /> <br /> Also, photons behave like particles in some contexts and like waves in others. Quantum physics is weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T12:56:22-08:00","id":776158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/776036-how-do-you-play-with-total-darkness#post776036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if there were any illumination anywhere it would be impossible to have an area with a &quot;total lack&quot;, because light bounces around (or works as waves I think, photons and all that).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always imagined total darkness to creatures of the night would be a setting in which even an animal with extremely good low-light vision (not infrared or ultraviolet) is blinded; actual (okay, figurative) cthonic darkness.<br /> <br /> That said, unless it's something the <i>characters </i>will have to deal with on a frequent basis, I'd count two layers of good light-proofing as sufficient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T17:55:53-08:00","id":776315,"title":"","content":"Closets people. Closets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T18:20:37-08:00","id":776339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/776036-how-do-you-play-with-total-darkness?p=776315#post776315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Closets people. Closets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just make sure to tuck a towel under the door.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T22:51:22-08:00","id":776441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/776036-how-do-you-play-with-total-darkness?p=776339#post776339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just make sure to tuck a towel under the door.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> and around the edges of the door... (seriously never seen a closet that was remotely light pollution proof)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T23:14:09-08:00","id":776452,"title":"","content":"I have. Then again, shit ain't half as poluted here as in the northern hemisphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T11:29:19-08:00","id":776692,"title":"","content":"A closet inside an already dark room inside an already dark building.<br /> <br /> I would go for the setup thing. Total darkness shouldn't be something so precise in measurement terms, but it should be something very unlikely to be found naturally in any above-ground environment, and even a little hard in underground artificial environments. The box inside a second box inside a third box during night seems the best configuration for me to start with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T23:16:38-08:00","id":780415,"title":"","content":"I'd go with the simple rule that if it is dark enough that a normal human would have to make an effort to detect the presence of an obstruction more than a few yards away it is dark enough. Since in most closets you would not be able to actually _see_ most things I'd count it as &quot;total&quot;, even if there is light you can see coming in from under the door.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T03:23:07-08:00","id":780475,"title":"","content":"I ignore scientific definitions and assume that someone's just exaggerating. &quot;Total darkness&quot; to me means that unaided human sight can't pick up details easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T05:25:46-08:00","id":786656,"title":"","content":"I strongly disagree with that, but not for a scientific reason.<br /> <br /> The idea behind all of this is precisely that a Vampire have far better vision than a human being. So the rule have to demonstrate such distinction. A vampire should see perfectly in conditions where mortals have already marked difficulty, and only start to be hampered where a mortal shouldn't see almost nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T05:36:26-08:00","id":786660,"title":"","content":"Just apply common sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T11:39:14-08:00","id":786818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/776036-how-do-you-play-with-total-darkness#post776036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some powers talk about &quot;total&quot; or &quot;complete&quot; darkness, and in my experience this isn't that common. I've been in a cave when they shut the lights out, that's total darkness. I've lived in both the country and city, total darkness doesn't really exist in either, there is simply too much light pollution even when the lights are turned out. You might not even believe what you can see in the wilderness when the lights are out and there is no artificial lighting.<br /> <br /> How do you address this in your games?</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree with your understanding of total darkness and your examples of darkness are spot on. I too have been in a cave with the lights out and that is a perfect example. The inner sanctum of vampire layers should be similarly light free without the aid of electronics. If the lights from streetlights can get in then so can sunlight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Strix can take an area of complete darkness and make it more, deepening it until it is no longer the simple absence of light but a gateway to wherever the Strix first came from. Creating the gateway requires a total lack of illumination in an area of at least a cubic yard (or meter). </div> </div> </div>I believe the size restriction here is not to indicate how far the source of light can be, because if it is complete darkness there is no source of light, but complete darkness is held within barriers of light, be they spaces between walls of your house, the insides of the pipes, theaters with the power off, or that basement with aluminum foil over the windows and blanket against the crack under the door. In a world filled with light, complete darkness only exists in such vessels, or around a several bends leading to an unlit chamber. Given this nature of total darkness, it makes sense to apply a size limit because otherwise gateways could happen EVERYWHERE because small places of complete darkness exist everywhere. I would rule strictly it must be at least a yard in all three dimensions, not some other thinner shape that adds up to a total volume of a cubic yard. That cuts off small pipes and most gaps between wall and makes the problem difficult but still manageable for those that are diligent. Otherwise you might as well say they can appear inside any building no matter how is it constructed.<br /> <br /> This is especially important because of the wispy shadowy nature of Strix it is easy to imagine them slipping through the smallest cracks.<br /> <br /> Fun thought of the day: The power lines that keep all those lights working in the building where you are at any particular moment of the day, they run through the complete darkness between most walls.<br /> <br /> I also with the strict definition of : Complete absence of of visible light, because that is very common, just not in sizable spaces. I mean I carry one around everyday in the stainless steel water bottle with opaque black plastic lid that screws on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-15-2015, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T11:41:19-08:00","id":786821,"title":"","content":"Thank goodness there's such a thing as Influence: Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T13:40:36-08:00","id":786910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank goodness...</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you are thanking the incorrect cosmic forces, but I complete understand your sentiment. It is very useful for the storyteller such things exist when they are painting a scene which evokes terror and dismay of this players.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-15-2015, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T16:16:31-08:00","id":787015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/776036-how-do-you-play-with-total-darkness?p=786818#post786818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I totally agree with your understanding of total darkness and your examples of darkness are spot on. I too have been in a cave with the lights out and that is a perfect example. The inner sanctum of vampire layers should be similarly light free without the aid of electronics. If the lights from streetlights can get in then so can sunlight.</div> </div> </div> </div>and street lights of course aren't the only thing I'm thinking about, I turn off my tv, my computer, etc, I can still see to walk without a flashlight? why all of these things have bright %$@ LED's on them that are on when powered down. So light pollution is not necessarily just about sunlight proofing it's about dealing with the infinite number of things connected and disconnected (cellphones) from power lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T16:36:12-08:00","id":787021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> and street lights of course aren't the only thing I'm thinking about, I turn off my tv, my computer, etc, I can still see to walk without a flashlight? why all of these things have bright %$@ LED's on them that are on when powered down. So light pollution is not necessarily just about sunlight proofing it's about dealing with the infinite number of things connected and disconnected (cellphones) from power lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree, which is why my statement included the caveat of<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">without the aid of electronics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those ubiquitous LEDs you mention, the faces of digital clocks, other such light-polluting electronics were exactly what I had in mind when I included that phrase. One flipped breaker, sliced wire, or blown fuse can render a room that is light-proofed against exterior light (like a standard vampire sleeping chamber, or even a movie theater) completely dark when the aforementioned go out.<br /> <br /> As a side thought, have you guys and gals seen the movie: <i>Vanishing on 7th Street</i>? This conversion really reminds me of that movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}